namespace BGE

  ' Distance fog for a `Camera3d` (its `fog`), sharing the draw distance's fade band
  ' (`Camera3d.drawDistanceFadeFraction`). Off by default.
  '
  ' With a `backdropHeight`, the band of the screen from where the ground ends up to that height
  ' at the draw distance (or the horizon, if lower) is filled in `color` behind everything, so objects fading out fade into
  ' fog rather than the sky. Drawables with `castsFogSilhouette` set keep blocking the sky past
  ' the draw distance, in `color`, out to `silhouetteReach` times it: an image as its screen box,
  ' a model as up to three boxes up its height (a tower on a nave), level walls
  ' (`BGE.DrawableWalls`) as their real outline.
  '
  ' Fog fixes the draw distance: it doesn't change with the render quality level (see
  ' `followsQuality`).
  '
  ' Fields are read every frame, so they can be changed live.
  '
  ' @example
  ' camera.fog.enabled = true
  ' camera.fog.color = &h1C2842
  ' camera.fog.backdropHeight = 400
  ' houseModel.castsFogSilhouette = true
  class Fog

    ' Nothing is drawn or worked out while this is false
    enabled as boolean = false

    ' RGB (0xRRGGBB), like `Drawable.color`
    color as integer = &h808080

    ' How high the backdrop reaches at the draw distance, in world units (0 for no backdrop). It
    ' never reaches above the horizon.
    backdropHeight as float = 0.0

    ' An `roRegion` stretched over the backdrop, tinted with `color` (so draw it white), or
    ' invalid for a solid band. One that's clear at the top softens the backdrop's top edge.
    backdropRegion as dynamic = invalid

    ' An `roRegion` stretched over each silhouette box whose top is open sky, tinted with `color`
    ' (so draw it white), or invalid for solid boxes. One that's clear at the top softens the
    ' silhouettes' top edges; boxes are cut so a softened top never shows inside a silhouette.
    silhouetteRegion as dynamic = invalid

    ' Silhouettes reach this many times the draw distance (0 for none). 1 keeps the fog that
    ' fading objects fade into without drawing anything past the draw distance.
    silhouetteReach as float = 2.0

    ' Fog makes up the opacity a fading object has lost, once its fade alpha drops below this
    ' (0 to 1): a model's box is drawn behind it at 1 - its alpha, and walls get solid fog
    ' under them, so wall and fog add up to fully opaque. Lower it to start the fog later in
    ' the fade band, which costs less but shows a step where it starts.
    silhouetteStartAlpha as float = 1.0

    ' With fog on, the draw distance stays at `Camera3d.maxDrawDistance` at every render quality
    ' level, so the fog's edge never moves. Set this to let it shrink at lower levels again, for
    ' speed: it then eases over `qualityTransitionSeconds`, so the fog creeps rather than jumps.
    followsQuality as boolean = false

    ' Seconds a draw distance change takes to ease in while `followsQuality` is set, when longer
    ' than `Camera3d.drawDistanceTransitionSeconds`
    qualityTransitionSeconds as float = 4.0

  end class

end namespace
